# Where the app talks to. Copy this file to `.env` and adjust.
#
# `.env` is git-ignored, so this example is the only thing that survives into
# the next session — which is the whole reason it exists. On 2026-09-10 a
# restarted Metro dropped this variable when it was passed as a shell prefix,
# the app silently fell back to the production URL baked into
# `src/config/env.ts`, and sign-in failed with "route api/v1/auth/login could
# not be found" because the API v1 branch is not deployed there. Twenty
# minutes went on the wrong end of that. Put it in a file; Expo loads it.
#
# 10.0.2.2 is the Android emulator's alias for the host machine's loopback, so
# this reaches an `artisan serve` running on the host at port 8090. A real
# handset on the same network needs the host's LAN address instead.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8090/api/v1

# ── Google sign-in ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Both ids come from ONE Google Cloud project, and they are not
# interchangeable:
#
#   ANDROID client — created with this app's package name
#                    (com.jambofilms.app) and the SHA-1 of the signing
#                    certificate. This is what proves a request came from
#                    this app rather than an imitation of it.
#   WEB client     — the one the website already uses. It is the fallback
#                    for anything that is not an Android build.
#
# Whichever the sign-in was made with ends up in the token's `aud`, and the
# server accepts either — see `services.google.client_ids` in the Laravel
# config. Set GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID there too, or the app's tokens are
# refused as "not issued for this app".
#
# Left EMPTY here on purpose. An empty value hides the Google button rather
# than drawing one that cannot finish, which is the bug this whole feature
# exists to fix. Filling them in locally does nothing useful anyway: the
# local Laravel has no GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, so `/app/config` reports the
# feature off and the button stays hidden.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
